# Frantic Scapegoat: "Haste. When this creature enters, suspect it" (CR 701.60a, 702.10a). Bot1's Scapegoat enters, its trigger
# suspects it (it has menace and can't block, CR 701.60c) and, with haste, it attacks the turn it came: Bot2 takes 1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Frantic Scapegoat
Plains x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Frantic Scapegoat.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Frantic Scapegoat.Suspected = (absent)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Frantic Scapegoat.Suspected = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Frantic Scapegoat.Keywords = CantBlock; Haste; Menace
Bot1.Attack(Frantic Scapegoat > Bot2)
[T1 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield.Frantic Scapegoat.Suspected = true
